      "id": 1,
      "text": "Columbia was founded as Smithton in 1819, then moved and renamed in 1821 because of a poor water supply.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://library.missouri.edu/missourian/columbiabeat/facts/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Boone County Courthouse, built in 1858, sits in downtown Columbia and became the county seat on April 7, 1821.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://library.missouri.edu/missourian/columbiabeat/facts/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Columbia College, the first college for women west of the Mississippi, was founded in 1839 and later became the University of Missouri.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbia%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The University of Missouri’s research reactor, the largest in the United States, supplies radioisotopes for nuclear medicine nationwide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
